#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ivm - incus VM launcher.

Reads VM templates (`<root>/templates/<name>.yaml`) validated against
`<root>/template.schema.json`, and drives incus from the HOST (no ansible/python in
the guest). Design: roles/incus_vm/REDESIGN.md (esp. section 8) +
roles/incus_vm/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.

Implemented: `init` (name prompt -> launch -> mounts -> provision: install
baseline+groups+packages, create user, run post_install_script -> push
dotfiles); `shell`/`shell-user`/`shell-root`; lifecycle `start`/`reboot`/`stop`/
`delete`/`update`/`provision`/`resize`/`mount`/`push`/`overwrite-dotfiles`/`set-password`/`unset-password`/
`enable-user-sudo`/`disable-user-sudo`/`info` (target VM status/hw/mounts/storage); `env`; `list` (incus list passthrough);
`adopt` (tag a pre-existing/older-ivm VM into ivm management; requires `--name`).
VM-acting subcommands resolve the target by cwd, or take a global `--name <vm>`.
Linux on Debian/Suse/RedHat families (apt/zypper/dnf). init = create stopped ->
attach devices (mounts + `shadow` masking, `hw.tpm`, macvlan/bridge `net`) ->
start -> provision (`sys.timezone`/`sys.tmpfs`/`sys.ssh_server`, packages, `thirdparty_software`,
`post_install_script`) -> push dotfiles. Plus `hw.secureboot=false`, `snapshot`,
`gui`, and the lifecycle/shell subcommands. `hw.nested_virt` is host-gated (warn
only). `--dry-run` prints every mutating command instead of running it. GPU
(virtio/passthrough) is intentionally absent - incus can't do shared virtio-gpu
3D; see docs/incus-hardware-capabilities.md. Still TODO: parent-dir prompt,
shell completion, windows tier.
"""

